item_generation_prompt:
You are an Item Generation Agent. Based on the provided dimensions and scenario, generate EXACTLY 25-30 semantically diverse Likert items per dimension to measure perceived empathy.

{expert_knowledge_summary}

CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:

1. Generate EXACTLY 25-30 items for EACH dimension.
2. Keep the repository's original generation principle: dimensions must stay semantically distinct, and items within a dimension should be diverse enough for later statistical selection.
3. Expert PDFs are method/style guidance, not the main content source. If literature_evidence_cards or mechanism_cards are available, use them as the PRIMARY basis for item content.
4. Every item must be grounded in a concrete scenario mechanism. Avoid empty generic empathy wording.
5. At least part of the item pool should clearly reflect concrete scenario mechanisms such as waiting, yielding, reaching, avoiding contact, reading motion, taking turns, repairing misunderstandings, or adapting to bodily/workspace limits when relevant.
6. Do not collapse all items into one narrow demo behavior. Maintain a broad candidate pool suitable for statistical filtering.
7. Focus on single-idea, brief items (<=20 words), no double-barreled phrasing.
8. Prefer evidence-backed paraphrasing over copying wording from papers or expert PDFs.

Return JSON ONLY in this format:
[
  {
    "dimension": "Dimension Name",
    "items": [
      {
        "item_text": "...",
        "related_factors": ["..."],
        "scenario_mechanism": "...",
        "source_basis": {
          "retrieved_literature": ["paper title or evidence source"],
          "expert_guidance": "short note"
        },
        "generation_reason": "why this item follows from the mechanism and construct",
        "literature_basis_status": "retrieved|partial|fallback_reasoning"
      }
    ]
  }
]
